    "Practical information | Univerzita Pardubice\nSkip to main content\nPractical information\nGetting to Pardubice\nWhen you fly to the Czech Republic, you will probably arrive at Vaclav Havel Airport in Prague, the capital city of the Czech Republic. At the airport you will find information about transport from airport to the main train station in Prague (Praha hlavní nádraží). The easiest way is the EA bus line (Airport Express): the bus stop is in front of the Arrivals hall.\nAt the main station, trains from Prague to Pardubice depart frequently (check times\nhere\n). The journey takes approximately one hour.\nYou can also fly to the Pardubice Airport. From this airport you can take bus number 90 connecting the terminal and main train station (Pardubice hlavní nádraží). The bus departs every 30 and 60 minutes after scheduled flight arrivals.\nFrom Pardubice’s station you can get to the University of Pardubice campus by taking bus number 3, 33 or 17 (the stop \"Terminál Univerzita\" is in front of the University Library). Another possibility is bus number 30 and 16 (the stop \"Univerzita\" is located in the centre of the University campus).\nWhen you arrive in Pardubice\nThe first thing you will probably do, is to check in at the dormitories (the reception is in building KC). A map of the campus you can\nfind here\n.\nYou will get an information e-mail from the Erasmus faculty coordinator indicating the date of your faculty welcome meeting. Participation in the welcome meeting is very important, as you will then receive a lot of necessary information.\nGetting online on the campus\nInstructions to get on the university wifi are available\nhere\n. Just switch into English. In case of any troubles with getting online do not hesitate to contact our IT department or your buddy student. To get online you will need your student access data indicated on your university Student ID card. You will get your Student card from your Buddy student just after your arrival. You will be contacted by him/her in advance.\nOrientation week\nThe week before each semester starts, there is an Orientation week that will help you to integrate into the Czech way of life and the academic system. During this week an intensive Czech language course is held and you can attend it for free.\nESN Pardubice\nYou will be contacted by your buddy from the ESN Pardubice before your arrival. They can pick you up at the train station and guide you to your accommodation and inform you about activities during the semester. ESN will make your experience at the University more enjoyable.\nLearn more about ESN.\nYou can also see their web\nesnpardubice.cz\n.\nInsurance\nHolders of EU Insurance can register after their arrival at a Czech Insurance company for free (essential care only). You can do so, for example, at the insurance company\nVZP\n.\nAfter your arrival, you can register at their\noffice in Pardubice\n: Karla IV. 73, 530 02 Pardubice.\nYou have to bring following documents with you:\nYour ID\nYour EU insurance card\nConfirmation of study at UPCE\nUniversity of Pardubice\nMap\nContacts\n​\nContacts\nFaculties and Central Services and Facilites\nPanoramic view\nExchange/Erasmus+\nInternational students\nMagazine MY UPCE\nWebsite feedback\nServices\nAccommodation\nLibrary\nDepartment of Physical Education and Sports\nNostrification\nE-shop\nThe Centre for Technology  and Knowledge Transfer\nLanguage Centre\nGuidebook for Internationals\nEuropean University Alliance\n© 2023\nUniversity of Pardubice\n,\nStudentská 95\n,\n532 10\nPardubice 2\nPhone:\n+420 466 036 111, 466 036 112, 466 036 113\nWebmaster\n,\nRSS\nData box ID:\nf5vj9hu\nAccessibility Statement\nCC BY-NC-ND 4.0"
